# Forms & Validation

## UiForm Pattern

All forms use `UiForm` from `@/components/form` with `react-hook-form` + `zod`:

```tsx
<UiForm<TInput, TOutput>
  schema={schema}
  defaultValues={defaultValues}
  onSubmit={onSubmit}
  ref={formRef}
>
  <FeatureView />
</UiForm>
```

## Field Components

Use ONLY these wrappers inside forms — never raw `<input>` for form fields:

- `FormInput` — `@/components/form/fields/form-input`
- `FormSelect` — `@/components/form/fields/form-select`
- `FormTextarea` — `@/components/form/fields/form-textarea`

Pass the schema input type: `FormInput<TLoginSchemaInput name="email" … />`.

## Schema Factory Pattern

```ts
export const createLoginSchema = (messages: Messages) =>
  z.object({
    email: z.email(messages.Auth.loginValidation.email.required),
    password: z.string().min(8, messages.Auth.loginValidation.password.min),
  });

export type TLoginSchema = ReturnType<typeof createLoginSchema>;
export type TLoginSchemaInput = z.input<TLoginSchema>;
export type TLoginSchemaOutput = z.output<TLoginSchema>;
```

- Schema file: `schema/{name}.schema.ts`
- Default values: `type/{name}.type.ts` exporting `{name}DefaultValues`
- Component builds schema: `create{Name}Schema(useMessages())`
- Validation messages come from i18n — never hardcode error strings.

## Buttons in Forms

Use `Button` from `@/components/ui` with `type="submit"` for form submission.
Use `loading` prop for async submit states.

## Refusals

- Do NOT use `@hookform/resolvers` directly in features — `UiForm` handles it.
- Do NOT use `yup`, `joi`, or other validators.
- Do NOT skip `TInput`/`TOutput` generic types on `UiForm`.
